.TH PDFX 1 "October 2026" "PDFX 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdfx \- High-performance Terminal & CLI PDF Swiss Army Knife for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfx
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBPDFX\fR is a lightweight, memory-efficient, keyboard-friendly Terminal & CLI application written in modern Rust for Linux.
It provides comprehensive PDF management including merging, splitting, extraction, rotation, page reordering, compression, text extraction, OCR, and an interactive Ratatui TUI viewer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output result in machine-readable JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open \fR[\fIFILE\fR]
Launch the interactive Ratatui TUI PDF viewer.
.TP
.B info \fIFILE\fR
Inspect document metadata, version, encryption, page dimensions, and page count.
.TP
.B merge \fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR... \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Merge multiple PDF files into a single document atomically.
.TP
.B split \fIFILE\fR \fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Split a PDF into separate files by page range (e.g. '1-5', '1-2,3-4', 'odd', 'even').
.TP
.B extract \fIFILE\fR \fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Extract specific page ranges into a new PDF document.
.TP
.B rotate \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR] [\fB\-a\fR \fIDEGREES\fR] \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Rotate pages in a PDF document (allowed angles: 90, 180, 270 degrees).
.TP
.B delete \fIFILE\fR \fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR [\fB\-y\fR]
Delete specific pages from a PDF document.
.TP
.B reorder \fIFILE\fR \fB\-s\fR \fIORDER\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Reorder document pages using 1-indexed comma-separated list (e.g. '3,1,2,4').
.TP
.B text \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR]
Extract text content (format: 'plain', 'json', or 'jsonl').
.TP
.B compress \fIFILE\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Optimize and compress PDF streams and prune unreferenced objects.
.TP
.B ocr \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-l\fR \fILANG\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPAGES\fR] \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Run OCR on scanned PDF pages to generate searchable Sandwich PDF.
.TP
.B clean [\fB\-\-history\fR] [\fB\-\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Clean local SQLite history, completed job records, and temporary files.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completion scripts (bash, zsh, fish, powershell).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid argument, syntax error, or page index out of bounds.
.TP
.B 3
Input error (input file does not exist or unreadable).
.TP
.B 4
Output error (permission denied or cannot write).
.TP
.B 5
PDF engine error (corrupted structure or password required).
.TP
.B 6
OCR engine error (Tesseract missing or execution failure).
.TP
.B 7
Operation cancelled by user.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Launch interactive TUI viewer:
.RS
.B pdfx open document.pdf
.RE
.PP
Inspect document structure in JSON:
.RS
.B pdfx \-\-json info report.pdf
.RE
.PP
Merge multiple documents:
.RS
.B pdfx merge ch1.pdf ch2.pdf ch3.pdf \-o complete_book.pdf
.RE
.PP
Extract text from odd pages to standard output:
.RS
.B pdfx text document.pdf \-p odd
.RE
